    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Ant Center\nSTUDIO\nHONOLULU",
      "THE HONOLULU ADVERTISER\nFriday, April 25, 1958.\n49\nPan American Airv\nTA STEWARDESSES FETED-Pan American World Airways was host I:\nght at a champagne party at the Reef Hotel marking the third anniversa\nthe entry of American-Japanese girls into the PAA hostess organizatir\ntown are Cynthia Tsujuauchi, Ruth Befu, Jean Izuo, Eileen Nakata, Ja\nongo, Reiko Kodani, Yuri Nakamoto, Jane Sakata, Carollyn Arizumi a\narion Tagawa.T0",
      "Many of the vintage PAN AM bags were donated from MR.\nYOSHIHISA MAYEDA's estate by his daughter, Carol Kuroda.\nMr. Mayeda was Director of Sales-Japanese Department\nOverseas Division. Pictured above are Mr. Mayeda with Ernie\nAlbrecht, Sales Executive of PAA - Hawaii. Standing are Pan\nAmerican stewardesses: Carolyn ArizumiJean Izuo, Reiko Kodani,\nCynthia Tsujiuchi, Yuri Nakamoto, Jane Sakata, Jane Hongo\nMasako Murakami. Ruth Befu Wakai. Aileen Nakata Sodetani."
